      "title": "wifi-nan: fix the AMBTT appearance and Discovery Beacon info",
      "message": "wifi-nan: fix the AMBTT appearance and Discovery Beacon info\n\nThe AMBTT (Anchor Master Beacon Transmission Time) is\nthe lower 4 octets of the Anchor Master TSF.\nSince the TSF is presented in little endian, it is\nconfusing to see the AMBTT in big endian.\n\nIn addition, better detect and present a Discovery Beacon.\nAccording to NAN spec (3.3.8.1), a Discovery Beacon interval\ncan be somewhere between 50 to 200 TU (Time Units).\nHence, Detect a Discovery Beacon if the interval is not 512 TU,\nand not only if the interval is 100 TU.\n",
      "author_name": "Triebitz, Shaul",
      "author_email": "shaul.triebitz@intel.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-06-30T09:50:15.000+03:00",
      "committer_name": "shaulTriebitz",
      "committer_email": "shaul.triebitz@gmail.com",
